      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It definitely generates friction when trying to join an event, especially if you have a lot of groups.\n\nThe current process is:\n\n- Get notification\n\n- Navigate to groups menu\n\n- Scroll until you find the group you're looking for\n\n- Click on group\n\n- Go to instances page, and join\n\nIt would be better if it was something like:\n\n- Get notification\n\n- Click join instance button",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-02-18T10:51:12.798Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Whenever you get a notifications from a group that there is a new event. It feels like a bit of an oversight that there is no button to take you directly to that event. You can now see the text and image for the event, unsubscribe from the group notifications and acknowledge/dismiss the notification.\n\nIf you're actually interested in the event There is a lot of friction where you need to search up the group first and then check the groups calendar. Especially if you have like 30-50 notifications to go through on a Friday. Which results in (at least for me) that I often don't do it due to it being annoying. Especially when you often get into the event and see that it's taking place 04:00 in the morning and you can't attend anyway.\n\nIt would be super nice if we had a third button to take us directly to the event that we got a notification for. So we easily can add it to our in-game calendar so we can remember it. I would even go so far and remove the unsubscribe button from the event notification and place it on the group page instead. (I have misclicked that button a few times.)",
